{"c":[{"id":"94d9cdb89929ed3f","sum":"W3: caret-bridge reaches the host over XPC, never page.sock; accept.ts needs --sign-identity (and --other-identity) and boots out its temp launchd host; headless CfT focuses a CDP-created window and activateTarget won't move it back.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204321Z-903b513efe20fc90","text":"W3: caret-bridge reaches the Caret host over XPC (CaretBridgeXPC), never page.sock; no <sock>.key exists. accept.ts needs --sign-identity <team SHA-1> (and --other-identity for refusal checks) and runs caret-bridge-testhost as a temporary launchd job it boots out.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204321Z-98052ff285eab267","text":"W3: headless Chrome for Testing gives focus to a window CDP Target.createTarget opens and Target.activateTarget does not move it back; chrome.windows focused is reported in headless. Page window focus = active tab of the focused, last-focused window.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"569740c12f8fdab5","sum":"W3, memory: a client's setCodeSigningRequirement guards replies, not its first send, so XPCHostLink sends nothing before a verified reply; personal memory is markdown in <dir>/Memory, the real folder only without --data-dir.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204321Z-a08d2817ff5ece3d","text":"W3: NSXPCConnection.setCodeSigningRequirement on the client blocks what it receives, not its own first call; whoever owns the Mach name sees open's arguments, so XPCHostLink sends nothing until a verified reply.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204904Z-98cc6d5ebfceb30a","text":"Personal memory is markdown (helper/src/memory): MemoryStore(dir) keeps it in <dir>/Memory unless told otherwise, and main.ts uses ~/Library/Application Support/Caret/Memory only when --data-dir is not given, so tests and evals never open the real folder.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
